## Recording-clock evidence map

| Approximate SRT time | Event and evidence boundary |
| --- | --- |
| ~00:00–00:02 | Show intro/tea advertisement and **staged interrogation recap** asking heroes what happened: this is creative out-of-game summary/framing, **not verified arrest, imprisonment or another in-world interrogation**. |
| ~00:02–00:06 | **Next morning** after S1E09. At finishing school **Margaret Dupayton** uses **Nolzur's Marvelous Pigments** from Evelyn's possessions to paint a convincing **Evelyn-shaped dummy in bed**, allowing Evelyn to skip the **noon bronze-ball planning session**. This is **actually performed** cover, superseding S1E09's merely considered Alter Self plan. Evelyn exits via window; a custodian is cleaning muddy fountain from her earlier mishap. The ruse has **not been proven to fool Lady Vestal**. |
| ~00:06–00:18 | **Krandal**, following a restless night at Pelor's temple with audible **overnight hammering** toward Hall of Penance, feeds the small mouse in his quarters and visits the **bronze-rank guild library**. The tabaxi **Hiroshi** lets him in and directs him to military/Elven codes. He finds a **possible Elven lantern code**: held/short taps could correspond to phonetic Common approximation **“eisth / eist(h)”** (GM spells E-I-S-T-H), but **cannot yet decide if the scheme matches or what it means**. Other code books do not match. He keeps the paper. The hammering/repair work is observed but no **finished mosaic restoration** shown. |
| ~00:18–00:26 | **Koh wakes beside his unconscious wife** and uses fresh-rest **Psionic Whispers**, with a **two-hour connection** selected. Instead of familiar written/mental speech he enters a vivid dark mental environment, seeing her as an apparently conscious **half-elf** by a flower. **Wife's spoken name sounds “Anthela/Anthea”**, ASR spelling uncertain. They **embrace, speak**; she says she has been there as long as she can remember, fears **“they'll know you're here,”** and believes **“they” want only her**, so **everyone in town will be safe if she stays**. **Deep drone** grows; **sand/dunes** close around Koh and he is forced from the scene. Back in bedroom, his wife's fists briefly clench and **physical black sand falls from her hands**; **Koh collects a pinch in an empty vial**. **Actual attempted psychic contact and material evidence occur**, unlike S1E09's intention only. The mental vision is experienced, **not objectively verified geography or the identity of her captors**; no wakeup/cure or independent sound link proven. He privately promises rescue and leaves with care arranged for daughter **Penelope**. |
| ~00:26–00:38 | **Eight AM full bronze-rank guild briefing**, led by ratlike **Jimmy**; Cassius and Carrie have **departed for Guild Academy/divination experts**. **Peaceful investigation** of ancient ruins **occupied by intelligent/sentient communities**, explicitly **not extermination**: self-defense permitted if attacked but teams asked to withdraw if talks fail. **Viper Gang** to goblins (rotten meat/climbing kit), **Brigand Patrol** to kobolds (cheese/eggs), **First Sons Brotherhood** to bullywugs (ham and straw hats), **Darkest Delvers** to **kuo-toa** (stinky fish and freshwater pearls), other **Five Emissaries** present but exact destination not independently established here. Each receives borrowed **city horse**, gift basket and rudimentary translation sheet (“yes,” “no,” “peace,” “want,” “above water”). **Clearstone** provides small boxes of **stirge-repelling “Sturge-ronella” incense cones** (lemongrass/garlic/wormwood/wild gourd; **three per Delver**, **30 minutes each**, claimed efficacy only). **The +1 armor, +1 shield, customized heavy crossbow** ordered in S1E09 are collected at Arcane To Go **before departure**; no longer pending after this montage. **Horn of Blasting and earlier guild-submitted samples have NOT been returned**, confirmed during underwater exploration. |
| ~00:38–00:48 | Horses prove unfamiliar to satyr Koh and to Evelyn riding with courtly side-saddle habits, but all eventually mount. **Krandal rides especially well**. Four-hour eastward horseback trip past first farm into lakeside swamp; approx **noon arrival**. No exhaustion confirmed; Koh's discomfort is roleplay. During ride Krandal describes paper with code to companions. |
| ~00:48–00:52 | **Evelyn understands the Elven term** tentatively transcribed **“eisth”** as a **funeral dirge/lament, not merely a funeral**, older/high-elven conjugation. Krandal identifies the tapping monk as **Rianu Keeves**. **Koh discloses to companions** having encountered a similar **unresponsive** person's condition (he does **not explicitly reveal wife’s identity**), and says normal healing may not suffice. The code meaning is **possible translation, not decoded message or cure**. |
| ~00:52–01:00 | Enter swamp on horses. **Koh burns one of his three stirge-repelling cones**, but a **stirge attaches to Krandal's horse** despite smoke. Koh **throws a dagger, kills stirge, retrieves dagger** without alerting oblivious Krandal; do not assert cones guarantee protection. A freshwater **catfish-like kuo-toa** spots the adventurers, flees toward lakeshore village; early attempt to call peace in translated word fails. |
| ~01:00–01:20 | Delvers dismount and approach **small lakeshore kuo-toa settlement** with ~**seven huts**, ~15 visible villagers, fishers, families/children (approximate GM count, not census). Evelyn presents **basket of rotten fish and freshwater pearls**; villagers gradually gather. Koh establishes **Psionic Whispers** with one elder and another villager, hoping to translate; elder takes involuntary speech as **divine revelation**, falls down, and community hails Koh as a god/being from **above (“swama,” phonetic)**. Koh repeatedly explains he is **not a god**, but veneration continues. Elder directs them to trader **Glepo Ma/Gleepo Ma** (phonetic spelling unresolved). |
| ~01:20–01:36 | **Glepo Ma**, a catfish-like kuo-toa in human-made trousers and soleless shoes, **speaks some Common**, runs a small **barter shop** hung with assorted salvaged objects and tells of growing up around a **circus**; unlike others he does not appear to worship Koh. In exchange for **Koh's shovel** he explains that nearby **ancient ruins lie underwater**, more accessible at **nightfall/low water** (exact tidal mechanics in a freshwater lake not established), and requests party fetch **a staff**, mentioning troubling **“big blee-blub/big blubs”** (term uncertain; not a confirmed named creature). Party plans early look rather than wait through daylight; they do **not yet retrieve requested staff**. Glepo Ma offers to care for horses and gives **Koh a small fishing rod** in a further barter, accepts their horses while villagers also revere them. |
| ~01:36–01:53 | At lake, party first swims **without potions** to assess. They deliberately **leave heavy equipment at shore**: **Krandal's +1 scale mail**, **Evelyn's newly enchanted +1 chain armor and Vicious hammer**, and Koh's bow/backpack remain near horses/in Glepo Ma's care. **Evelyn keeps Goat of Travail figurine and javelins**, Koh retains **studded leather, enchanted climbing sash, psychic blade and drift globe** among light kit. **Gear is not lost/stolen**, but remains behind at cutoff; no automatic in-cave armor protection. Koh spots a sunken chest that proves a **slow-swimming aquatic mimic**, escapes without combat. **Glepo Ma already knows it**, says to swim away. The mimic lives and returns to chest form. |
| ~01:53–02:03 | Ruin entrance roughly **130 feet offshore**, **20 feet beneath surface**. **All three drink their one Water Breathing potion**, effect **one hour** each in session; Koh begins fresh **one-hour Psionic Whispers** to communicate underwater. Thus S1E09's purchased potions **are consumed** and cannot be listed as unused. Underwater building has same **ancient design and trap order** as forest/city structures. Floodwater holds spear/pit traps in altered position; darts float overhead. This establishes **architectural relation/repeated layout, not a fully verified physically continuous dungeon**. |
| ~02:03–02:12 | Koh and Evelyn discover familiar concealed **stone chest** behind algae-covered secret-wall button; Krandal helps open. Inside **a stone-metal Ring of Protection** with archaic Elven inscriptions. Koh activates/identifies it mentally: **+1 AC and +1 to all saves, usable by any**, not soulbound. With others' consent, Koh **passes ring to Krandal, who actually puts it on left middle finger** (and later speaks of wearing it). **Six psychic-responsive spear shafts** remain in adjacent room: **party decides to leave them in place until possible departure**, no proof they were taken at cutoff. Also GM confirms **earlier guild trophies/horn not returned**. An out-of-character late character-sheet **long-rest button click** is bookkeeping, **not a sudden new in-world rest inside underwater room**. |
| ~02:12–02:21 | Underwater **pit shafts connect into a deeper passage**, leading after minutes to partially air-filled cavern with small flame torches and yet another deep pit. Party chooses to surface in cavern before probing lower black hole. Across pool on ledge they see a **kuo-toa ritualist** worshipping a wall carving of **three bumps connected by a line and a spiral beneath**, with **dark ooze/sludge seeping from cracks**. He has a **conch-decorated homemade staff**, wand and stone-symbol amulet. **Whether this glyph is identical to every previously seen motif or merely related awaits audio/map verification**; GM calls it familiar. |
| ~02:21–02:39 | When Evelyn surfaces noisily, ritualist sees party, grasps staff and **attacks**, creating a **~50-foot violent whirlpool/vortex**. Koh is sucked below, takes **two separate 8-bludgeoning-damage hits**; attempts to anchor climbing sash to cavern ceiling and succeeds **via thrown dagger as an anchor aid**, not by making sash float or attach to empty air. Ritualist's dark Sacred Flame fails as Koh dodges. **Krandal casts Command (“grovel”)**, forcing creature prone one turn but **GM rules its vortex concentration survives**; no automatic spell-ending claim. Evelyn swims/uses current to close distance; one unsuccessful long-range javelin shot. |
| ~02:39–02:55 | Koh **escapes whirlpool by climbing anchored sash**, then hooks rope around ritualist to **zipline toward him**. Krandal casts **Bless on Koh**. Evelyn rides vortex like a torpedo, lands **nonlethal unarmed blow (5 damage)**; Koh strikes with **psychic blade (13 damage)** and **shortsword butt/nonlethal intent (5 damage)**, breaking vortex concentration. Ritualist **survives**, casts **Tongues** and pleads for mercy. No killing, incapacitation by unconsciousness or body mutilation established. Evelyn gives Koh **10 Lay on Hands HP**; party **takes staff and wand**, and Koh's sash restrains ritualist. |
| ~02:55–03:04 | Bound ritualist's name sounds **“Big Blee/Bleeber Bloops”** (uncertain, not canonized spelling). Claims he is there to **“connect”** with a god he has been without, and the carving refers to **“the Dunes”**, a place **“where the god rests”**, sleeping **“for now”**. These are **an NPC's religious claims**, **not independent confirmation of Enzo's Dawnless Dunes, wife's realm, god's identity or cosmic truth**. Claims staff is his **self-made object**, not an Elven artifact; conch, rope/feathers visibly assembled, yet channels magic. Krandal wonders whether killing him would prevent dangerous worship; Koh argues **against executing an unarmed defeated captive**, and companions choose **to bring him back to Glepo Ma for judgment/consultation**, not murder. They rig enchanted sash into harness/backpack on **Krandal's back**, **start return intent**, but **DO NOT reach surface, village or guild before cutoff**. Sash now engaged restraining prisoner, not lost. |
| ~03:04–03:06 | **Out-of-game episode end and network outro**, GM explicitly teases whether group **will reach surface with fish wizard**, showing **no safe escape yet**. **Water Breathing timer remains a live constraint** from ~one-hour window; no claimed expiry, next-day rest, staff delivery, encounter with additional “big” creature, final reward or fish-village decision. |

## High-impact continuity and custody

- **Major change from S1E09: Koh ACTUALLY CONTACTS wife in dark dune vision**. Descriptions of her motives, captive bargain and 'they' belong to her **vision testimony**; waking-world **black sand physically emerges from her fists**, Koh collects **pinch in vial**, her body still does **not awaken**. **Krandal and Evelyn hear only that Koh knows a similar unresponsive case**, not explicit wife identity. Disturbing drone parallels temple, but linkage is unproven.
- **Rianu Keeves finger signal:** Krandal's provisional lantern-code reading **“eisth”** interpreted by Evelyn as **a dirge/funeral song**, not a full decoded message or verified cure; note both name and transliteration await audio.
- **Peace mandate and fish village:** Guild wants **evidence of ancient Elven ruins without massacre of residents**; **Koh misidentified as god** by villagers after psychic speech, repeatedly denies it. Glepo Ma speaks Common and requests a staff from submerged ruin. **No ruling that villagers accept Koh's denial or that staff was delivered.**
- **Krandal's Ring of Protection:** Physically **worn by Krandal**; +1 AC and saves, transferable. **His +1 scale mail left by horses**, not carried into lake. **Evelyn's +1 armor enchantment, Krandal's +1 shield and face-decorated crossbow are completed and picked up in departure montage**, but heavy armor/shield location versus worn underwater is distinct. Gear on land guarded by villagers/shopkeeper but **not verified secure at end**.
- **Water Breathing:** **Each of the three potions drunk** before descent; **one-hour countdown** in play. Koh's second/new telepathic group connection also lasts **one hour**. Stirge-repellent cones **not guaranteed**, one burned and one attached stirge killed on ride.
- **Captured ritualist:** **Alive, restrained and carried by Krandal at scene cutoff**; homemade conch-staff/wand disarmed, custody with party but exact individual bearer unshown. **Dark ooze beside rune** observed; meaning unknown. **Other six psychic shafts left in secret room** and no quest completed/reward paid.
- **Next source:** **Delvers S1E11 — No More Fish**; do not preempt return from episode title.

